John H. wrote:

> It probably shouldn't be that easy to steal from shops, but I question
> the current way it's handled.

I've always found it a bit strange that shopkeepers don't mind pets
and random monsters walking in, taking their stuff and leaving.

Seems as if they should at least try to bar pets from entering 'No
[pet]s allowed, [sir/ma'am].', treat any object held by the pet as
payment pending (immediately bar the door), and if the player tries to
stand in the doorway and use their pet to fetch, bar the pet from
leaving the shop the same way they would a player (giving them a free
move if necessary if the player stands on the tile in front of the
door).  Using a magic whistle to pilfer goods from a shop should
summon the Keystone Kops.

Monsters shouldn't pick up goods owned by a shopkeeper unless they
have some means of escaping with it, and this could have some
interesting consequences -- although I know having non-tame monsters
attacking one another (and even just having the game remember who
stole what) would be tricky business.  Might also be interesting if
monsters could pay for items in gold, assuming they have it (just
direct move the gold from the monster's inventory to the shopkeeper's
when the monster picks the item up).

